# Per-address limit on NEW TCP connections to 80 and 443 (the only rate limit of the Sepolia runbook; see
# docs/client/indexer-hosting.md, "Rate limiting: the option taken"). Its own table: ufw's rules are not touched.
# It limits connections, not requests: one HTTP/2 connection carries many requests. It is also per port, not per site,
# so it covers every site Caddy serves on this VPS. 30 new connections a second per address, burst 60, is far above a
# browser's use (a few connections per page view) and well below what a flood needs.
table inet paved_ratelimit {
	chain input {
		type filter hook input priority -10; policy accept;
		tcp dport { 80, 443 } ct state new meter paved_v4 { ip saddr limit rate over 30/second burst 60 packets } counter drop
		tcp dport { 80, 443 } ct state new meter paved_v6 { ip6 saddr limit rate over 30/second burst 60 packets } counter drop
	}
}
